<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 7-yr govt bond avr price set at 102.22 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 7-yr govt bond avr price set at 102.22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of Hungary's seven-year government bonds, issued for the first time, was set by auction at 102.22 percent of the face value, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday  HTBL.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     8,750 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     35,782 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    8,749.99 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 9,625 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum price		     101.81 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     102.22 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price		     103.00 pct </p>
<p>NOTE - The bond bears a floating interest, calculated on March 20 and September 20 every year adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on September 24. The starting interest is 25.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
